              "label": "WHAT DOES THE BST INVARIANT BUY YOU?",
              "placeholder": "",
              "required": true,
              "reveal": {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "At each node, keys in the left subtree are ordered before the node key and keys in the right subtree are ordered after it under the chosen duplicate policy. A key comparison therefore tells you which child subtree can still contain the target.",
                "progressive_reveal": {
                  "spans": [
                    {
                      "id": "left",
                      "text": "left subtree",
                      "required": true
                    },
                    {
                      "id": "which",
                      "text": "which child subtree can still contain the target",
                      "required": true
                    }
                  ]
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "real-use",
              "kind": "connects_to",
              "label": "REAL USE: IN-MEMORY ORDERED INDEX",
              "placeholder": "",
              "required": true,
              "reveal": {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "An ordered in-memory index can support exact lookup plus predecessor/successor-style operations when implemented with a balanced search tree. The BST invariant supplies the search rule; balancing is what keeps height logarithmic in production-quality ordered trees.",
                "progressive_reveal": {
                  "spans": [
                    {
                      "id": "ordered",
                      "text": "ordered in-memory index",
                      "required": true
                    },
                    {
                      "id": "balance",
                      "text": "balancing is what keeps height logarithmic",
                      "required": true
                    }
                  ]
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "warning",
              "kind": "not_this",
              "label": "A PLAIN BST IS NOT AUTOMATICALLY O(log n)",
              "placeholder": "",
